@*
    The header and footer keep their rows because their content is their
    minimum size; the clipped list between them has none, so it shrinks.
*@
<div class="page">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="stack">
            <div class="heading"> header — a visible row keeps its height</div>
            <div class="list">
                @for (var i = 1; i <= 200; i++)
                {
                    var n = i;
                    <div class="line"><span class="muted">@($"{n,4} ")</span>an overflowing list; overflow: hidden makes its minimum zero, so it is the one that shrinks</div>
                }
            </div>
            <div class="heading"> footer — so does this one</div>
        </div>
        <div class="side">
            <div class="heading">in a row, text shrinks to its longest word</div>
            <div class="pair">
                <div class="blue">short words wrap freely here</div>
                <div class="red">an unbreakableidentifier holds</div>
            </div>
            <div class="muted">the red box cannot go narrower than "unbreakableidentifier", so the blue one gives way first.</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
